Hi $firstName,

Your Synapse account ($userName) is scheduled to be disabled in 15 days, on $expirationDate, due to inactivity.

To meet our FISMA-MODERATE requirements, Synapse accounts are disabled after a period of inactivity. This helps us protect user data, maintain security, and ensure that only active accounts retain access to Synapse resources.

If your account is disabled:

    You may lose access to Synapse projects, data, and tools associated with your account.

    Collaborators may be impacted if they rely on your account’s access or permissions.

    Reactivation may require additional steps to verify your identity and restore access.

To understand the full impact and details of account expiry, please review our help article here:
 Help article: [Link to help doc]

If you would like to keep your account active, you can reset the expiry countdown by signing in before [expiry date]:

    Go to the Synapse sign-in page:
     Sign in:

    Sign in with your existing credentials.

    Once signed in, your account expiry countdown will be reset automatically.

If you believe you received this message in error, or if you have questions about your account status, please contact us through Synapse Support.

Thank you for being part of the Synapse community.

Best regards,



The Synapse Team
